//! Tablet I/O for `rmu hub` behind one trait, [`Tablet`]: the lock, the
//! watchdog, stopping and starting xochitl, the cloud-pairing guard, the
//! stat pass, streaming download, verification reads, the tablet state
//! file, staging and the staged apply (see `docs/hub-design.md`).
//!
//! Two implementations:
//!
//! - [`SshTablet`], the real one, over [`crate::ssh::SshSession`]. Every
//!   operation is one round trip running a script generated by a pure,
//!   unit-tested function in `scripts`. Scripts go over stdin (`sh -s`),
//!   so file lists are not bounded by the remote command line; the
//!   transfers (download, staging, state write) put a short command on
//!   the command line and their data on stdin.
//! - [`FakeTablet`], over two local directories, with simulated xochitl,
//!   boot id and watchdog, and fault injection for the end-to-end tests.
//!   It shares the lock format, staleness decision and apply ordering
//!   with the real one, so both honour the same contracts.
//!
//! **Guard.** Every mutating operation takes the [`HeldLock`] returned by
//! [`Tablet::acquire_lock`] and first checks, on the device and in the
//! same invocation, that the watchdog has not fired and that the lock
//! still names this run, under a `flock` held to its last change (see
//! `scripts`). The apply script repeats the check before every document.
//! A run whose watchdog fired, or whose lock was taken over, therefore
//! stops at its next mutation ([`DeviceError::WatchdogFired`],
//! [`DeviceError::LockLost`]). Exceptions: starting xochitl checks only
//! the lock (bringing the UI back is always allowed to the holder), and
//! staging checks the guard without the `flock` (it is a network
//! transfer into the run's own directory).

mod apply;
mod fake;
mod lock;
mod scripts;
mod ssh;

